    "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/louisiana/northwesternstate/jobs/5519442/associate-director-of-bands-and-assistant-professor-of-music": {
      "title": "ASSOCIATE DIRECTOR OF BANDS AND ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OF MUSIC",
      "description": "ASSOCIATE DIRECTOR OF BANDS AND ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OF MUSIC Salary $73,000.00 Annually Location Natchitoches, LA Job Type Unclassified Job Number 999540 Department Northwestern State University Opening Date 10/16/2026 Description Benefits About this Job Northwestern State University is currently seeking qualified applicants for the position of Associate Director of Bands and Assistant Professor. This is a 12-month position at the rank of Assistant Professor tenure-track position and is commensurate with experience and qualifications. Anticipated start date of July 1, 2027. Review of applications begins immediately. To Apply: Review of applications will begin immediately. Deadline: December 1, 2026 Please send the following materials via email in one PDF file: application letter, vita, transcripts (unofficial at this time), names and contact information for five references, links to a marching band and/or concert band rehearsal (and performance if possible), and other appropriate credentials to: Mr. Scott Burrell, Director The Dear School of Creative and Performing Arts Northwestern State University Natchitoches, LA 71497 Email: capa@nsula.edu Notice of Non-Discrimination (Full Disclosure) Northwestern State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws. This policy applies to all terms and conditions of employment, including recruiting, hiring, placement, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, transfer, leaves of absence, compensation, and training. All complaints or inquiries related to Title IX should be directed to the Director of Title IX Compliance and Title IX Coordinator, Julie Powell (318-357-5570), Room 306 of the Friedman Student Union or email tix@nsula.edu. In accordance with Section 35.106 of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), all participants, applicants, organizations, and interested individuals are advised and noticed that the ADA Coordinator for Northwestern State University for facilities is the Director of University Affairs, Jennifer Kelly (318-357-4300), located in Room 128 Caspari Hall or email andersonje@nsula.edu. For student academic services, contact the Director of Accessibility and Disability Support, Crissey Smith (318-357-5460) located in Room 111 Watson Memorial Library or email smithcr@nsula.edu. For faculty/staff accommodations and services, contact Executive Director of Institutional Effectiveness and Human Resources, Veronica M. Biscoe (318-357-6359), Room 111 Caspari Hall or email ramirezv@nsula.edu. Minimum Qualifications 1.Minimum degree-Masters required; doctorate preferred; 2.Evidence of successful teaching experie??ce at high school and/or the college level with marching bands and concert bands. Job Duties and Other Information Duties and Responsibilities Teaching Direct all aspects of the Spirit of Northwestern Marching Band. Oversee faculty and student leadership of the Purple Haze Basketball Pep Band. Conduct the Fall Winds concert ensemble (fall semester) and the Wind Ensemble (spring semester). Teach courses based on the candidate’s qualifications and departmental needs, including undergraduate conducting and a student leadership and development course. Improving Teaching, Assessment, etc. Teach online, in-person, and hybrid courses. Demonstrate knowledge of program goals and objectives. Submit course outlines and objectives. Maintain class schedules. Provide course instruction in accordance with the developed syllabus. Advise/mentor students. Utilize a variety of proven teaching methods appropriate to targeted domains of learning. Evaluate students and report progress. Participate in periodic review of course materials. Scholarship Maintain appropriate expertise and competencies through continuing professional development and pursuit of scholarly activities. Participate in scholarly activities, including grant writing, research, scholarly publication, and presentations. Service: Band Program Administration/Activities Assist the Director of Bands in fostering an environment and culture that inspires students to grow and supports the educational focus and institutional objectives of the band program and university by attending and participating in all marching band-related events. Actively recruit prospective students through a variety of activities and initiatives on and off campus; actively engage with outreach efforts to public school band programs throughout the region. Coordinate and lead efforts for successful athletic band recruiting events, including Young Performers Day and Classic on the Cane Marching Festival. Assist with band area scholarship auditions, contracts, renewals, etc. Work with the Director of Bands to coordinate performances, tours, and programming for all related band activities. Serve as faculty advisor/co-advisor to either Kappa Kappa Psi (KKY) or Tau Beta Sigma (TBS) band service organizations. Maintain and update the athletic band program’s presence and information on the departmental website. Assist the Director of Bands in the upkeep and oversight of program inventories, including athletic band instruments and marching uniforms. Coordinate and supervise students and staff for the annual Summer Music Camps. Attend and collaborate in band staff meetings and maintain open and collaborative communication with colleagues. Attend campus-wide meetings representing the band staff as requested by the Director of Bands. Service: Departmental/University/Profession Actively participate and represent NSU, CAPA, the Department of Music, and the band program at state, regional, and national conventions as needed. Establish and maintain positive relationships with stakeholders, the instrumental faculty, ensemble directors, and other departments/programs across campus. Participate in departmental faculty meetings and serve on all appropriate programs and committees in the Dear School of Creative and Performing Arts and Department of Music. Serve as a Graduate Faculty Member and chair/serve as a committee member of graduate student committees and guide graduate research as requested. Maintain confidentiality in accordance with federal laws and policy. Engage in professional service. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the Director of Bands, Department Chair, or CAPA Director from assigning additional duties that logically relate to the position. Benefits for unclassified employees are determined by the individual hiring authority. Employer State of Louisiana Address 1201 N 3rd St Baton Rouge, Louisiana, 70802 Phone (866) 783-5462 Website http://agency.governmentjobs.com/louisiana/default.cfm"
    },
    "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/louisiana/northwesternstate/jobs/5532487/assistant-professor": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR",
      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR Salary $65,000.00 - $72,000.00 Annually Location Shreveport, LA Job Type Unclassified Job Number 998871 Department Northwestern State University Opening Date 10/28/2026 Description Benefits About this Job Northwestern State University is seeking a 12-month full-time, tenure track faculty position in radiologic science within the School of Allied Health available in Shreveport, Louisiana. The position will begin upon selection of a qualified candidate. INTERNAL APPLICANTS ONLY. The position will remain open until filled. Review of applications will begin immediately. Only complete applications will be reviewed. To Apply: Submit a letter of application, current CV, official transcripts (if not from NSU) along with three professional references to: Ms. Becky Farmer, Department Head for the School of Allied Health, Northwestern State University, 1800 Line Avenue, Shreveport, LA 71101-3127 or email to brittb@nsula.edu . Inquiries regarding employment applications should contact the individual department: Department: School of Allied Health Telephone: 318-677-3020 Notice of Non-Discrimination (Full Disclosure) Northwestern State University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws. This policy applies to all terms and conditions of employment, including recruiting, hiring, placement, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, transfer, leaves of absence, compensation, and training. All complaints or inquiries related to Title IX should be directed to the Director of Title IX Compliance and Title IX Coordinator, Julie Powell (318-357-5570), Room 306 of the Friedman Student Union or email tix@nsula.edu. In accordance with Section 35.106 of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), all participants, applicants, organizations, and interested individuals are advised and noticed that the ADA Coordinator for Northwestern State University for facilities is the Director of University Affairs, Jennifer Kelly (318-357-4300), located in Room 128 Caspari Hall or email andersonje@nsula.edu. For student academic services, contact the Director of Accessibility and Disability Support, Crissey Smith (318-357-5460) located in Room 111 Watson Memorial Library or email smithcr@nsula.edu. For faculty/staff accommodations and services, contact Executive Director of Institutional Effectiveness and Human Resources, Veronica M. Biscoe (318-357-6359), Room 111 Caspari Hall or email ramirezv@nsula.edu. Minimum Qualifications Master's degree required, preference given to master's degree in radiologic sciences, however a doctorate is preferred; Eligible for LA license as Radiologic Technologist and at least two years clinical experience as a registered technologist required; Teaching experience at the college level preferred; Shall be credentialed and in good standing by relative credentialing agencies, if appropriate; proficient in curriculum development, instruction, evaluation and academic counseling; Qualified to teach in field of study and effective in teaching the assigned subject material; And shall meet the required standards defined by the University. Job Duties and Other Information •Demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching, scholarship, service, and professional growth. •Teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses in face-to-face, hybrid, and online learning environments. •Develop, revise, and deliver course content that aligns with program, college, university, and accreditation standards. •Submit course syllabi, objectives, assessments, and other instructional materials in accordance with university policies and established timelines. •Utilize evidence-based instructional strategies and educational technologies to promote student engagement and learning. •Evaluate student performance and provide timely feedback regarding academic progress. •Participate in periodic review, assessment, and continuous improvement of courses, curricula, and academic programs. •Assist with the collection, analysis, and reporting of program assessment and student learning outcome data. •Support accreditation activities, including compliance reporting, self-studies, and site visit preparation, as assigned. •Provide instruction and supervision in laboratory, simulation, and clinical learning environments, as appropriate. •Assist with the supervision and evaluation of student clinical experiences in collaboration with clinical affiliates and program leadership. •Promote compliance with university, programmatic, clinical, and safety policies and procedures. •Serve as an academic advisor and mentor to students, providing guidance regarding academic success, professional development, certification, licensure, and career opportunities. •Participate in student recruitment, retention, progression, and graduation initiatives. Benefits for unclassified employees are determined by the individual hiring authority. Employer State of Louisiana Address 1201 N 3rd St Baton Rouge, Louisiana, 70802 Phone (866) 783-5462 Website http://agency.governmentjobs.com/louisiana/default.cfm"
    }
